# Title: ETW Trace Evasion Activity
# ID: a238b5d0-ce2d-4414-a676-7a531b3d13d6
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: @neu5ron, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community
# Date: 2019-03-22
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1070, attack.t1685, car.2016-04-002
# Description: Detects command line activity that tries to clear or disable any ETW trace log which could be a sign of logging evasion.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((cmdline:*cl* AND cmdline:*/Trace*)) OR ((cmdline:*clear-log* AND cmdline:*/Trace*)) OR ((cmdline:*sl* AND cmdline:*/e:false*)) OR ((cmdline:*set-log* AND cmdline:*/e:false*)) OR ((cmdline:*logman* AND cmdline:*update* AND cmdline:*trace* AND cmdline:*--p* AND cmdline:*-ets*)) OR (cmdline:*Remove-EtwTraceProvider*) OR ((cmdline:*Set-EtwTraceProvider* AND cmdline:*0x11*)))
